      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CORMORAN STRIKE NZ (6) is hard to knock having made it four wins and a placing from his last five starts here when he came from this same barrier to score by 2.3m last time. Drops back to the mile but has won his last two attempts at the distance. Looks tough to beat again. GANDHI MAIL ITA (8) has chased Cormoran Strike in both outings since winning his local debut but he had little luck two back before leading from this barrier last start and sticking on for second. He can give a sight again. PESCO POLLO (7) disappointed last time but had scored twice in a row prior. Has won five of eight tries at the mile so the distance drop should suit. RAKERO BLAZE NZ (10) hasn't raced since July's Inter Dominion series where she struggled with her manners but she has been readied for her return with a trial win.",
